Subject: Tillerbook cutover - what happens between 18 and 21 September and what you need to do

INTERNAL - for all Ombrellick staff

Hello everyone,

This is the main notice about the move from our old Granary ERP system to Tillerbook. Please read it all. It affects every site.

1. THE CUTOVER WINDOW

Granary ERP will be switched off at 19:30 on Friday 18 September 2026. Tillerbook will be available from 05:00 on Monday 21 September 2026. That is a window of 57.5 hours with no enterprise system.

The final go or no-go decision will be made by the Chief Information Officer on Thursday 17 September at 16:00, after the third dress rehearsal. If the decision is no-go, the fallback weekend is 2 to 5 October.

2. FREEZES BEFORE THE CUTOVER

- Purchase orders: no new purchase orders can be raised after 17:00 on Wednesday 16 September. Urgent orders during the freeze need a paper requisition signed at the correct delegation tier.
- Supplier payments: the last payment run in the old system is on Tuesday 15 September.
- Payroll: Tessaway Plains pay period 19 will be processed two days early. Pay dates do not change.
- Member accounts: statements will not be available online during the window.

3. WHAT HAPPENS AT THE SITES DURING THE WINDOW

- Harrowgate Elevator: the weighbridges keep working on paper dockets. Use the pre-numbered docket books in the weighbridge office (books 4401 to 4460). Dockets will be keyed into Tillerbook by Wednesday 23 September.
- Stellmoor Creamery: tanker intake is recorded on the offline intake sheets. Milk testing results are held in the laboratory system as normal.
- Pellam Bay Cannery: production and retort records are not affected. They are on the plant control system, which is not part of this change.

4. YOUR NEW SIGN-IN

You will sign in to Tillerbook with your usual staff user name. You must set a new password at first sign-in.

Your new password must meet the current Access Control and Password Standard. In particular it must meet the minimum length in that standard, which is longer than the old one, and you will be asked to register a second factor on your phone or a key fob. Passwords from the old system will not be accepted.

Shared sign-ins on plant-floor terminals stop working at cutover. Every operator needs their own badge. If you do not have one, tell your supervisor by Friday 11 September.

5. TRAINING

Everyone who uses the system must finish the 40-minute online module before cutover. At the time of writing, 587 of 965 staff have finished it.

Classroom sessions for purchasing, weighbridge and payroll users:

- Harrowgate Elevator training room: 8 and 9 September
- Corrin House, Room 2.14: 10 and 11 September
- Stellmoor Creamery canteen annexe: 14 September
- Pellam Bay Cannery boardroom: 15 September

6. GETTING HELP

During the first two weeks after cutover, the Service Desk will be staffed from 05:00 to 22:00 every day including the weekend.

- Extension: 4417
- Email: servicedesk@ombrellick.example
- Floor-walkers in orange vests will be at each site from 21 to 25 September.

Please do not phone members of the project team on their personal mobiles. Use the Service Desk so that problems are logged.

7. ONE WARNING

We expect scam emails pretending to be from the Tillerbook project. We will never ask for your password by email or phone. If you receive such a request, report it to the Service Desk and do not reply.

8. A NOTE ON COST AND SCOPE

Several of you have asked. The project budget approved in the capital programme is $3.26 million, and spending to the end of July was $2.71 million. The member app (version 4.12) goes live on the same weekend. The plant control systems at the three sites are out of scope.

Thank you for your patience. This is the largest systems change the Society has made in 17 years.

